Nova bundles or derives from the following third-party works:

1. fate — https://github.com/babyname/fate
   License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017 godcong
   Use: naming rules, scoring weights, 八十一數理 / 三才 tables and interpretation text
   (transcribed and converted to Traditional Chinese by tools/transcribe_fate.py), and
   resources/character.json as the base character dictionary (slimmed by tools/build_chars.py).

2. lunar-javascript — https://github.com/6tail/lunar-javascript
   License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 6tail
   Use: src/vendor/lunar.js, inlined into dist/nova.html for 農曆 / 四柱 / 生肖.

3. lunar_python — https://github.com/6tail/lunar-python
   License: MIT, Copyright (c) 6tail
   Use: Python reference implementation (nova_core/bazi.py); not shipped in the HTML.

4. Unihan Database — https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html
   License: Unicode License v3 (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt)
   Use: 康熙 radical/stroke (kRSKangXi), readings and definitions to validate and
   supplement character data at build time.

5. OpenCC (opencc-python-reimplemented) — https://github.com/yichen0831/opencc-python
   License: Apache-2.0
   Use: build-time Simplified → Taiwan Traditional conversion only; not shipped.

Big5 常用/次常用 character ranges are used (via Python's built-in codec) to derive
common-character levels; no Big5 table is redistributed.
